A||||24||skitime||Great day at the Reading PA POCI show.  (Pics)||||1||
Z||000000||skitime||09-23-2001||08:00 PM||||Today we all had a great day at the Reading PA POCI show.  We had 8 Fieros meet for breakfast and cruise to the show. The weather was great and we had 26 Fieros show up. Fieros had by far the most cars there. We impressed the show officials so much that they are giving us more Fiero classes for next years show. Cool. Thanks to all that made it to the show for making it such a good day<P>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P1010001_2.jpg">     <P>Checking out Rockcrawl's 4.5 Caddy engine install.  (Great job! Rockcrawl)And it is for sale too.<P>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P1010002_1.jpg">    <P>Gilberts and Mark talking Fieros<P>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P1010003_1.jpg">     <P>Eric_PA, Springtyme, and Rockcrawl checking out the class of stock Fieros<P>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P1010005_1.jpg">     <BR>Many of the modified Fieros<P>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P1010010.jpg">     <BR>Mark Hoagland's beautiful very rare yellow 88 GT T-Top with lumbar and subwoofer.<P>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P1010012.jpg">     <BR>More discussions on the Caddy engine install.<P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-1.JPG">     <P><p>[This message has been edited by skitime (edited 09-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||rockcrawl||09-23-2001||08:41 PM||||Yes, It was a great time. I got to catch up with a bunch of old aquaintances and meet some great people for the first time too. It's great to finally meet people who I have heard so much about.<P>I told Vonnie to delete that picture with me in it! I even moved out of the way so she could take another one. Well at least I wasn't picking my nose or something!||||reg||1
Z||000002||grgoyl86||09-23-2001||08:57 PM||||We had a <B>GREAT</B> turnout at the POCI show today. There were thirteen (YES, <B>13!</B>) Fieros in the stock Fiero Class, and NINE Fieros in the Modified class. There were also six "other" cars in the mod class. So, including the "just visiting" Fieros, there were 26 Fieros in a show with a total of 73 cars. That's over a third of the entire show! (BTW, these numbers are my observation, not official numbers.)<P>The POCI folks were so impressed that they agreed to make two stock Fiero classes next year, as well as a separate Modified Fiero Class. This is cool, as no other model had its own Mod class this year.<P>We also found out that the Keystone State Chapter of POCI has it's 2002 shows pretty much planned. The Spring show will be in Pottsville, and the Fall show will be back at AW Golden in Reading. No dates that I heard yet.<P>OK, what you've all been waiting for, the winners. Congrats to all:<P><FONT SIZE="3"><B>Class H, Fiero</B></FONT><BR>	1. Veronica Houck<BR>	2. Frank Sombers<BR>	3. Mark Hoagland<BR>	3. Jim Gilbert<P><FONT SIZE="3"><B>Class J, Modified</B></FONT><BR>	1. Denny Lambert<BR>	2. Jason Haughey<BR>	3. Dave Horst<P><FONT SIZE="3"><B>Longest Distance Traveled</B></FONT><BR>	Joe Rebilas, from State College, PA<P><BR>Special thanks go to Jen Gilbert, Joe Rebilas, Denny Lambert, and Bruce Walters for volunteering to help vote. That also helps our image with the POCI folks.<P>We'll let you know when the pictures are posted.<P>Coming up in the MAFOA area:<BR>	Tech Day at Windswept Acres in Oley, PA on October 6.<BR>	POCI Show in Greenbelt, MD on October 14<P>Check out the Calendar page on <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieropride.com</A>  for more info and other events.<P><B>Bob Schlag</B><BR>Mid Atlantic Fiero Owners Association<BR>New England Fiero Association <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieropride.com</A><P>------------------<BR><B>Bob Schlag</B><BR><I>Mid Atlantic Fiero Owners Association</I><BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieropride.com</A><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ani_interior.gif"> ||||reg||3
Z||000003||jimmybpei||09-23-2001||09:12 PM||||Hey guys,<P>looks like lots of fun too bad there wern't <BR>more fiero up here on pei canada. the biggest turnout we woul get are my 3 haha.<P>Rockcrawl <BR>how long have you had the caddy motor in for and have you had any major buugs to work out <BR>would like to know as my goes in mon nite as soon as i get off work.<P>Skitime <BR>havent heard from you on the forum in a while<BR>Still seriously considering  carlise in the spring. I've gor a long winter of construction to the yellow car before then.<BR>If it doesn't get done i'll just take the caddy, indy whatever<P>Later <BR>Jimmy B<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||grgoyl86||09-23-2001||09:13 PM||||Here are some of my pictures:<P>Here's the "Scene of the Crime"<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P9230015.JPG"> <P>Here's an overview of the show. Look at all the Fieros!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P9230002.JPG"> <P>Looks like Flea Bit Dog was playing Cops and Robbers!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P9230003.JPG"> <P>Some of the Fiero folks found some shade to hang out in:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P9230001.JPG"> <P>||||reg||12
Z||000005||skitime||09-23-2001||09:21 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by jimmybpei:<BR><B><BR>Skitime <BR>havent heard from you on the forum in a while<BR>Still seriously considering  carlise in the spring. I've got a long winter of construction to the yellow car before then.<BR>If it doesn't get done i'll just take the caddy, indy whatever<P>Later <BR>Jimmy B</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey I am still here but back to work too. You know you have a place to stay if you do come to Carlisle.  BTW, if you drive that Indy down here you will have to fly home. We are serious about that.<P><p>[This message has been edited by skitime (edited 09-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Springtyme||09-23-2001||09:33 PM||||For it being a Pontiac, Buick, Olds show, Us Fiero's ran the whole show! It was great to meet everyone! =) I had a lot of fun, still kinda mad that the car that looks EXACTLY like mine (minus the luggae rack) got a trophy and I didn't =( Hehehe, j/k! It was great for my first car show! Thanks for the invitation too!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Springtyme.jpg"> ||||reg||10
Z||000007||Denny||09-23-2001||09:51 PM||||It was really nice seeing all the old friends, and making new ones, especially those from this forum. I had a great time!     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>As Bob said, as soon as we get the pictures posted . . .<p>[This message has been edited by Denny (edited 10-03-2001).]||||reg||10
